WEBVTT

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:23.870
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:31.210
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:38.980
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.790
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:57.570
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:04.540
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:12.480
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:20.150
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.450
Gee. Another accident in front of our station.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.310
Couldn't make the turn and hit the pole.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.790
That makes the ninth accident like this.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:50.350
Maybe it was true, then.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.910
There are rumors of sightings.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.560
Of what?

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.320
You don't know?

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.720
We're talking about
ghosts!

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.530
Give me a break. Nobody believes
ghost stories in this day and age.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.960
You're only skeptical because
you've never seen one.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.940
More than a few people have seen it.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.340
Their eyes were just playing tricks on them.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.180
Just don't let your guard down.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.540
Soon, it'll be sneaking up on you from behind.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.320
Hello.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.950
Hey, how's it going?

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.050
Another messy accident, huh?

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:24.880
You on the night shift?

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:28.890
Huh? Oh, no, I've been so busy lately,
I haven't had any time for myself, so...

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.460
I see. Well, just don't
overexert yourself.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.720
Thanks. Same
to you.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.890
See you.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:38.800
Nakajima.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.570
Getting back to what we were saying.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.540
What?

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.340
Oh, the ghost. If I run into it, I'll make
sure to tell it to stop loitering.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:59.420
What's the matter with those maintenance
people anyway? So...

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.430
Ghosts in this modern
day, huh?

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.200
Well. Better get
back to work.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.640
Aah!

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:21.400
This place is freaking
me out.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.910
What was that
just now?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.880
A-a-a...

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.920
A ghost!

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:41.930
FILE. 44
8OKUTO GHOST
STORY

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:42.400
"Traffic Section"

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.370
What? You're kidding,
right?

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.500
No, I'm not. He saw a ghost outside the
window and practically turned to jelly.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.470
Imagine! Seeing ghosts,
at his age!

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.410
He was probably just tired. He
has been on night shift a lot.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.610
And it's silly to think there are any
ghosts around these days, right?

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:05.390
The next guy into the men's room said that
for some reason the floor was soaked.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.590
You mean he pissed in his pants?!

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:10.620
You mean he pissed in his pants?!
Ah... Well, I won't be the one to say it...

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.160
I saw the ghost AFTER I'd
done my business!

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.360
This isn't a joke. I
honestly saw it!

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.570
You don't have to get
so upset about it.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:21.260
You must have been
exhausted, that's all.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.670
Believe me! I actually saw...

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.310
I believe you.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.430
Huh?

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:30.770
At night, spirits come to places where
people tend to congregate.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.610
And they sometimes hang
around car wrecks.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:38.080
You mean, you've
seen them, too?

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.220
No, that's not what
I'm saying.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.090
What is it?

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.660
There! Isn't
that...

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.400
Come on, tell me you're just
joking around here.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:53.670
Thought so.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.010
What?

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:58.030
I've been looking everywhere for this file!

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.000
Quit jerking us
around, okay?

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.410
I've seen the ghost
too, you know.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.420
A strange silhouette passed by me, on
a stairway that isn't used very often.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.140
I saw the same
thing.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:13.090
I've heard the sound of bare feet,
in the middle of the night.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:16.090
Nakajima's seen it two
or three times now.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.630
Maybe it's beckoning
to you!

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.600
N... no. It
is not!

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.600
Let's calm down and consider
this objectively.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.730
In this modern age, do you really believe
that there are spooks floating around?

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.900
There have to be simple explanations
behind these so-called ghosts.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:38.040
You know what they say..."Not all black
paint is the work of the Devil."

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.450
You mean, "the Devil is not
so black as he is painted."

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.790
That man has a serious problem.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:47.390
That man has a serious problem.
Hmm. I guess we're left with one choice.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:47.520
Hmm. I guess we're left with one choice.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.760
Which is?

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:53.720
What else?! Get the ghost out in the open!

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.690
"Traffic Safety"

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.040
I'm going to the store. You
guys want anything?

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.280
Can you get me some bug repellent?

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.680
Get me anything that'll ward off evil.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.840
Don't be stupid, you can't tell
her to get just anything.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:23.630
You want me, working overtime handling
all the complaints you've received...

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:28.620
...to stay here even longer,
and chase ghosts?!

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.900
Chief, it's painful to hear
you put it that way.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.560
Then try to imagine the
pain I'm feeling.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.610
Hey, Chief! Ready?
Say cheese!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:44.000
Do as you wish on your own time, but don't
confuse your private life and public duties...

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.580
This is our duty, Chief!

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:46.650
Huh?

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:51.180
This evil is trying to destroy our station.
Huh?

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:53.690
We must expose
the culprit!

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.220
Is that a
fact?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.360
Thank you very much!

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.020
In that case...

00:06:59.200 --> 00:06:59.860
Huh?

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:00.830
Yes?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.890
Don't get yourselves too
wrapped up in this.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.190
Hmm?

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:08.000
Do you know something
about this?

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.670
Yes!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.510
There's a scary old legend
about Bokuto Station.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.980
Uh, there is?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:26.250
It was in the Fifties, when Japan had begun
to pick itself up after the war.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:30.990
An officer was alone, on night
shift, in a police box.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.590
It had been pouring
rain all night.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:37.960
In the dull gloom, the officer
suddenly looked up.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.210
And there was an old man,
standing just outside.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:46.940
He had no umbrella and just
stood there, staring in.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.940
"Can I help you?" the
officer asked.

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.570
"I need directions."

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:56.280
The officer said it was too late to go anywhere.
But the old man didn't hear him.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.940
So the officer
had to help.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.920
<i>"Let's see."</i>

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.920
<i>"Wait, this mark</i>
<i>here..."</i>

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.530
<i>"Uh..."</i>

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:31.220
<i>"This marked place</i>
<i>is the..."</i>

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.120
<i>"...cemetery."</i>

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:36.050
Th-th-the man probably just
ran away, that's what!

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.160
But he was old,
remember?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:43.600
And don't forget that old people
can't move very fast! Right?

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:46.600
Guess I'd better get going to the store.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:49.110
Someone like my dad could run fast enough!

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:49.760
Huh?

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.270
<i>"I'm full of</i>
<i>gusto!"</i>

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.210
What are you talking about?!

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:56.680
What are you talking about?!
Yup, that's for sure!

00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:00.910
He certainly goes the dis-
tance to get off-topic.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:02.990
Do you know about the dummies
kept in the station warehouse?

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:05.820
"Traffic Safety Campaign"

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.290
You mean the ones used in
traffic safety classes?

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:08.430
"Traffic Safety Campaign"

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.420
Yes. But among those
dummies...

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.930
...there is one that should
never be used.

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:18.370
It's a dummy of
a little boy.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:23.410
One time, it was used in a demon-
stration of pedestrian accidents.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:32.450
<i>"As you can see, it's impossible for</i>
<i>cars to come to a sudden stop."</i>

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.850
"Traffic Safety Class"

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:34.880
<i>"As you can see, it's impossible for</i>
<i>cars to come to a sudden stop."</i>

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:41.380
<i>"Never cross a road without looking</i>
<i>first, boys and girls. Okay?"</i>

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:42.630
<i>"What's the matter?"</i>

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:45.360
<i>"Blood! Oh, Bleeding!</i>

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:48.530
<i>"What on</i>
<i>earth?"</i>

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:53.330
<i>"It hurts! Mommy,</i>
<i>it hurts!"</i>

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:02.340
You know, I've seen that old dummy
in the back of the warehouse.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:06.380
They do say that spirits
often inhabit dolls.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:10.850
Who cares? I'm never going to set
foot in that warehouse again!

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:16.260
Nakajima? Nakajima!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:20.500
Huh? What happened?

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.730
Pretending not to hear, huh?

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.930
It was about ten
years ago.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:29.660
It was a dreadful night,
humid and rainy.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.670
An officer of this station
was stabbed in an alley.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:40.580
Even though he was
gravely wounded...

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:44.140
...he tried calling us. But his
injuries were massive, and...

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:50.920
...before the phone could be answered,
his strength gave out.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:56.970
On muggy nights since then, the phone
will ring at that same moment.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:11:04.270
And the pleas of the slain officer can
be heard from the other end.

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:10.410
The phone will ring? But not the phone
here in the Traffic Section, right?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:15.740
I answer the phone quite a lot, but I've
never had that kind of call before.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:16.890
I have.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:17.410
What?

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.860
Why don't you get it, Miyuki?

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:26.600
You answer it, Nakajima.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.860
I think you'd better get it, Kobayakawa.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.000
You scared,
Nakajima?

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:33.000
Why should I be?

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:38.000
That's right. What would
he be afraid of?

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.670
Y... Yes?

00:11:55.960 --> 00:12:00.290
I'm scared! Come
get me!

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:17.450
The small hours
of the morning.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:22.950
That is when ghosts and monsters
descend upon the land.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:31.750
And wells are one place they
always appear.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:37.460
Wells are a bridge from this
world to the netherworld.

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:42.440
From ancient times, they were thought
to be the entrance to Hades.

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:47.440
This story centers around
such a well.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:58.450
There was a peddler who lived near Sumida
River, in the fine city of Edo.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.360
<i>"Go safely,</i>
<i>husband."</i>

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:05.090
<i>"Off I go, to sell</i>
<i>my wares."</i>

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.290
What on earth has he been
doing all morning?

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.130
Well, let's
continue.

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:16.030
<i>"See you."</i>

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:20.770
The man had recently married,
and led a life of bliss.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.850
<i>"It's going to be another</i>
<i>sweltering day."</i>

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:26.540
<i>"No time for banter,</i>
<i>Miss Yoriko."</i>

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:30.280
He was very honest and sincere,
which was good for business.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.440
His business was small,
but thriving.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:36.790
And he had a fine reputation
in the town.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:42.790
On the surface, it appeared as though the
man had no problems whatsoever.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:49.300
But as it turned out,
he had one problem.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:56.270
<i>"How depressing. I only intended to sell</i>
<i>during daylight, but before I knew it..."</i>

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:02.780
The man's problem was the road
he took on his return trip home.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.990
Along the way, he had no choice
but to pass by a certain place.

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:10.620
"Crime Announcement; This person was crucified
fortreason. - Justice Court"
The gallows, where criminals
were executed.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:14.690
<i>"I have to pass by it, otherwise</i>
<i>I can't get home."</i>

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:19.530
<i>"Perhaps... no! My beloved wife</i>
<i>is waiting for my return, and..."</i>

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.470
<i>"...I can't have her worrying</i>
<i>about me."</i>

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:25.630
The man was
a coward.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:29.440
But the thought of his bride gave
him the courage to go on.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:32.110
The man made up his mind,
and continued on his way.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.650
<i>"I mustn't look.</i>
<i>I mustn't look."</i>

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.300
And just
then...

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:49.800
<i>"Evening."</i>

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:51.330
<i>"Good evening,</i>
<i>sir!"</i>

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.490
<i>"I didn't hear a thing!</i>
<i>Not a thing!"</i>

00:14:57.610 --> 00:14:59.600
<i>"Please spare me</i>
<i>from death!"</i>

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:02.840
<i>"I'm not interested in</i>
<i>causing your death."</i>

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:03.770
<i>"Huh?"</i>

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:07.940
<i>"Perhaps you've mistaken me</i>
<i>for a ghoul of some sort?"</i>

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:12.720
<i>"My dear sir, I am but a mere</i>
<i>watermelon peddler."</i>

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:16.120
<i>"As you can</i>
<i>see."</i>

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:20.820
<i>"It's true. But why do you sell</i>
<i>your stock in such a place?"</i>

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.520
<i>"Edo stares coldly on strangers</i>
<i>like myself."</i>

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:26.600
<i>"But my goods are of</i>
<i>the highest quality."</i>

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:33.400
<i>"The first of the season.</i>
<i>Here, try some."</i>

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.610
<i>"It looks delicious. Are you</i>
<i>sure I can have it?"</i>

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:42.720
<i>"Certainly. If you like it, then you</i>
<i>can consider buying some."</i>

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:48.380
<i>"Seeing for oneself is better than</i>
<i>hearing 100 accounts. I'll try it."</i>

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:52.160
<i>"How is it?"</i>

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:56.160
<i>"Marvelous! I've never tasted</i>
<i>such sweet watermelon!"</i>

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.700
<i>"Happy to</i>
<i>hear it."</i>

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:02.630
<i>"I'll take two!"</i>

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.390
<i>"I'm home."</i>

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.890
"You've brought watermelon!"

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.220
<i>"The first of the season."</i>

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:22.660
"I'll put one in the well, to cool."

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.560
<i>"I bought them already</i>
<i>chilled."</i>

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:27.690
<i>"We can have this</i>
<i>one right away."</i>

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.230
<i>"Why aren't you having any?</i>
<i>Come on, it's delicious."</i>

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:14.140
<i>"Yes. I will have some.</i>
<i>Such a dark red."</i>

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:18.910
<i>"It looks delicious."</i>

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:25.010
<i>"Have another."</i>

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.490
<i>"Very good!"</i>

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.530
<i>"Is that all</i>
<i>there is?"</i>

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:44.640
<i>"What are you saying? You were so busy</i>
<i>enjoying it, you even ate mine."</i>

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:49.040
<i>"Oh, I'm very sorry. That</i>
<i>was terrible of me."</i>

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.680
<i>"Don't worry about it."</i>

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:56.240
<i>"Don't worry about it."</i>
<i>"I'll get the other one!"</i>

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:58.750
<i>"It's chilling in the well, isn't it?"</i>

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:01.720
<i>"It's chilling in the well, isn't it?"</i>
<i>"That's correct."</i>

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:07.760
<i>"But whether or not you could call that</i>
<i>thing in the well a watermelon..."</i>

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:13.530
<i>"...is quite another</i>
<i>matter, husband."</i>

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:20.740
Chief, enough with these
stories, all right?!

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:24.240
I suppose you're
right.

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:43.090
What a drag. Just a bunch of
stories, and no real ghosts.

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:46.190
What happened to my idea
of solving this mystery?

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:50.700
Really. And we didn't see anything while
the Chief was telling his stories.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.910
Guess we have nothing to worry about.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:54.380
Think so?

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:56.210
I know so.

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:57.850
Did you see?

00:18:57.850 --> 00:18:59.520
I did!

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:02.210
Something's out there! Isn't it?!

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:04.990
The balcony!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.790
Wait for me!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:08.850
See anything?

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:11.490
Mm-mm. I can't see down there.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:14.160
So maybe it was a ghost.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:17.390
Look at
that!

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:19.540
Footprints!

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:22.030
Footprints!
There shouldn't be footprints there!

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.310
They're ghost
footprints!

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:26.300
Do ghosts have
feet?

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.250
If they're not ghost footprints, what are they?

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.510
I don't know!

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:33.080
If it was a prank, there'd be handprints, too.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:36.210
If it was a prank, there'd be handprints, too.
I'm sure they're ghosts!

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:39.650
What do you think you're doing?!
Get out of my way!

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.690
I'm not in your way!

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.590
Just get off of me, would you?!

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:45.330
Toukairin.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.350
What?

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:50.970
Hey, what're you doing
here this late?

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:52.500
Look who's talking!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.800
What are you doing up there?

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:58.130
Who, me? Training. Just
what it looks like.

00:19:58.310 --> 00:20:00.640
I did this routine every day when
I was on the rescue team.

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:03.470
But why at this time
of night?

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:07.610
It's the only time I'm free. I've got so
many things to do in the daytime.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.290
Were you out here last night, too?

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:11.080
Yeah. Just about this time.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:12.620
I get it.

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:15.050
What a bungled
mess.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.990
You can't even tell the difference be-
tween a lieutenant and a ghost.

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.290
I don't believe
you!

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.290
Have I done something
wrong?

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:26.360
Not at all! You haven't done
anything wrong, sir.

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:28.090
The problem
is him!

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:34.800
At least the mystery is solved!
And that's a good thing!

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:36.170
Unreal.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:39.210
Which reminds me, haven't we
forgotten about something?

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.480
Now that you mention it...

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:41.950
Now that you mention it...
What's that?

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.850
They're
gone!

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:47.280
Where did everybody
take off to?!

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:51.990
"Traffic Section"

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.860
Kobayakawa!
Tsujimoto!

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:53.890
"Traffic Section"

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:57.830
Nakajima! Where did
everybody go?

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:00.570
They said they were
off to find a well.

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:02.860
A well?!

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:05.340
Maybe I went a little
overboard.

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:15.950
See anything?

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:17.990
Almost nobody ever comes here.

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:24.980
There's one! Look! Right over there!
Almost nobody ever comes here.

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:26.860
That thing?

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:28.230
That's the well.

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:29.500
So there really was one.

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:31.630
There you are!

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:32.860
Lt. Toukairin!

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.260
Sorry about
last night.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:37.460
No, I'm sorry for scaring
you like that.

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:40.940
I wanted to apologize, so I bought
this! See? A watermelon!

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:43.700
A ghost!

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:46.370
Hey! What's wrong
with you guys?!

00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:51.710
I never want to see another
watermelon again!

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:01.830
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:12.440
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:19.340
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:29.460
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:43.430
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.710 --> 00:22:51.650
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.710 --> 00:23:00.290
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:08.360
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:08.430 --> 00:23:17.940
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:25.380
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:33.710
It's been awhile since I've been
out driving with you, Natsumi.

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:36.290
Oh, it's Lt. Toukairin.

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:40.290
Oh no, those two! Where on
earth have they gone?

00:23:41.130 --> 00:23:42.190
What is this?

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:43.760
This is the grave
of my sempai.

00:23:44.800 --> 00:23:47.200
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 45...

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:49.440
..."A Summer's Day
Together."

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:51.810
Oh, a shower.
